      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+(-\\frac{1}{4})}{1-(-\\frac{1}{4})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-\\frac{1}{4}}{1+\\frac{1}{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{3}{4}}{\\frac{5}{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
